# AS_BUILT.md is an append-only log: every change adds an entry at the top, so
# two open PRs conflict by construction rather than by subject. Every resolution
# has been the same mechanical "keep both" — five rebases in one evening across
# four unrelated PRs at the worst of it, which is what motivated the (now
# reversed) one-file-per-entry split.
#
# `union` is git's built-in driver for exactly this shape: it takes both sides of
# a conflicting hunk instead of raising. Verified with a control before landing —
# the same two-branch merge conflicts without this line and resolves with it,
# both entries intact.
#
# It is correct here ONLY because the file is append-only. Union NEVER reports a
# conflict, so a change that genuinely rewrites existing lines gets silently
# doubled rather than flagged. A restructuring pass over this file wants a real
# review, not a merge driver.
docs/AS_BUILT.md merge=union
